  "query_preview": "..\nDistant Tropical Storm Dujuan continues to move farther north, away \nfrom the region. Dujuan is steering relatively drier air south of \n20N, leading to spotty showers across Tinian and Saipan, then showers\nbecome increasingly scattered across Guam and Rota, closer in \nproximity to the trailing monsoon surge. Scattered showers and \nisolated thunderstorms are expected to continue across Guam and Rota \nover the next several days, extending across Tinian and Saipan over \nthe weekend and early next week. The main band of monsoonal moisture \nlingers near and south of Guam, with model guidance showing some \npotential of a nearby weak disturbance forming in the monsoon trough \nearly next week. Depending on this scenario or if the monsoon shifts \nfurther north, this could potentially result in periods of scattered\nto numerous showers with moderate to strong gusts.",
